# =============================================================================
# office-ai — local environment template
# Copy to .env and fill in values for local dev.
# =============================================================================

# Nothing is required at runtime today — the Next.js editor and the
# `office-agent` CLI both run with zero env. This file exists so that
# release-pipeline secrets that DO need attention (and live on GitHub,
# not on disk) are at least discoverable from the repo root.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release pipeline (GitHub Actions only — NOT used by `make dev`)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by: .github/workflows/auto-release.yml (the optional
# `notify-downstream-host` job). Used to push a
# `chore(officeai): bump to X.Y.Z` commit into a downstream host repo
# on every successful office-ai release. Without this config, the
# release still succeeds as a standalone office-ai GitHub Release.
#
# These are GitHub Actions settings — do NOT put the token in a local
# .env file. The lines below are for documentation only.
#
# Where to get it (one-time, ~3 min):
#   0. Pick the downstream repository and lockfile path, then add:
#      Repository variable: OFFICEAI_DOWNSTREAM_REPOSITORY=owner/repo
#      Repository variable: OFFICEAI_DOWNSTREAM_LOCKFILE=infra/officeai.lock.json
#      The lockfile variable is optional; the shown path is the default.
#   1. Open https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#      (Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens
#       → Fine-grained tokens → Generate new token)
#   2. Token name:           OFFICEAI_SYNC_TOKEN
#      Resource owner:       downstream repo owner
#      Expiration:           1 year (set a calendar reminder to renew)
#      Repository access:    Only select repositories → downstream repo
#                            IMPORTANT: scope to the downstream repo,
#                            not office-ai. The secret LIVES in
#                            office-ai but AUTHENTICATES against the
#                            repo receiving the bump commit.
#      Permissions →
#        Repository permissions:
#          • Contents:  Read and write
#          • Metadata:  Read-only   (auto-selected; cannot be turned off)
#   3. Click "Generate token", copy the `github_pat_…` string.
#   4. Open https://github.com/jhoetter/office-ai/settings/secrets/actions
#      → New repository secret
#      Name:   OFFICEAI_SYNC_TOKEN
#      Secret: <the token from step 3>
#
# Verify by triggering a push to office-ai/main and watching the
# `notify-downstream-host` job in Actions: when configured, it should
# commit to the downstream repo's main branch without an auth error.
# Common gotcha: GitHub defaults the `Contents` permission to
# `Read-only` — flip it to `Read and write`, otherwise checkout will
# succeed but `git push` will fail with exit code 128.
#
# OFFICEAI_DOWNSTREAM_REPOSITORY=owner/repo
# OFFICEAI_DOWNSTREAM_LOCKFILE=infra/officeai.lock.json
# OFFICEAI_SYNC_TOKEN=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
